Rewritten: the provider profile (its OpenAI-compatible gateway at
https://api.experientiallabs.ai/v1, its key variables EXPLABS_API_KEY and
EXPERIENTIALLABS_API_KEY, its curated fallback model list and its auxiliary
vision model) as a Nodecode catalog row and a credential hook; and the
account-usage reads behind Hermes' /usage view (GET /credits and GET /key on
the Cost API, the wallet window and the daily key cap) as the /explabs slash
command, keeping the original's fail-open posture and its dollars-and-cents
formatting.

Left out, and why: Nodecode has no per-provider usage view for a cell to
fill, so the two reads answer a command instead of a panel, and the
4.5-second clamp the original applies to fit Hermes' 10-second usage hook is
not needed here (the setting stays, its ceiling does not). The original's
error classifier, which re-marks the gateway's transient guardrail 400s as
retryable, is left out because Nodecode's retry ladder reads the status
alone; a guardrail refusal therefore ends the turn with the gateway's own
message, and a second ask is the operator's. The live `GET /v1/models`
listing is not read either: the picker draws the curated fallback, as the
original does when its live read fails.
